<title>USA: American Banknote signs China phone venture.</title>
<headline>American Banknote signs China phone venture.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>American Banknote Corp said on Monday its Brazilian subsidiary will supply stored-value telehone cards for a new telephone system to be set up in the northern Chinese province of Shanxi.</p>
<p>The contract is part of a joint venture with two other Brazilian companies, privately-held Interprint and ICA Telecomunicacoes, and three governmental agencies in China to set up a telephone system using Telebras technology. The six partners expect revenues of $25 million to $30 million through 1998, said Morris Weissman, American Banknote's chief executive.</p>
</text>
